  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nIn the releases widget I have configured home assistant as an item to be monitored, the line for HA shows an error rather than the version number and when you click on the details it shows \"Only the first 1000 results are available\" as the error condition.  All other items setup in the widget appear normal right now.  I have seen this error in the past, typically only lasts for a few days but the Home Assistant has been showing this for multiple weeks across multiple versions of Homarr.\n\n<img width=\"286\" height=\"201\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c51c62a6-c279-4d45-a25f-a84b1cc4cc3a\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCurrently in Homarr version 1.74.0, Add the releases widget and configure home assistant as in the attached photo.  \n\n<img width=\"592\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3431f34f-824e-4ff3-a697-4296120958e5\" />\n\n### Impact\n\nNo workaround, minor annoyance - Homarr is still usable but shows inaccurate info for this specific item.\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_\n\n### Version\n\n1.74.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Run\n\n### Browser\n\nSafari",
